finding: attachTexture inherits attachView's stamp: 0 (src/core/rendering/view.ts:460), and pruneView ignores generation while stamp is zero (view.ts:492). A camera destroyed and recycled before its first draw leaves the old owned texture bound to the new camera instead of pruning/destroying it. Independently reproduced on HEAD with createApp(RenderPlugin), attachTexture, world.destroy(eid), world.create() (same eid), adding Camera/Transform, world.step(0): Views.get(newEid).texture === oldTexture is true. Record the live generation when binding texture targets and add a recycled-before-first-frame GPU assertion that observes destruction and no inherited target. The selected GPU test passes (1 test, 8 assertions, bgra8unorm) but only removes Camera after a presented frame, so it cannot catch this lifetime failure.
